 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Vinnie's race car flew over the grandstand, with his chicken on board.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.528
  },
  {
   "text": "He'd flipped its wing. \"Wings go UP!\" So why are race car wings upside down?",
   "s": 3.728,
   "e": 7.561
  },
  {
   "text": "Lap one: the car went light, like a shopping cart on ice.",
   "s": 7.861,
   "e": 10.549
  },
  {
   "text": "Henrietta, the team hen, was thrilled. She's wanted to fly since she was an egg.",
   "s": 10.748,
   "e": 14.523
  },
  {
   "text": "So Vinnie bolted on a second wing. \"Wings go UP!\"",
   "s": 14.723,
   "e": 17.34
  },
  {
   "text": "Lap two: the front wheels lifted. Dot, the driver, steered at clouds.",
   "s": 17.46,
   "e": 21.031
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the whole car took off, over forty rows of fans and a hot-dog stand.",
   "s": 21.231,
   "e": 24.678
  },
  {
   "text": "It landed in the hay bales, like a dart in a cushion.",
   "s": 24.878,
   "e": 27.296
  },
  {
   "text": "So what's the wing for? A plane's wing is curved to pull the plane up.",
   "s": 27.496,
   "e": 30.673
  },
  {
   "text": "Flip that same wing upside down, and it pushes the car down.",
   "s": 31.073,
   "e": 34.186
  },
  {
   "text": "More push, more grip. The tires bite into the corners.",
   "s": 34.386,
   "e": 37.041
  },
  {
   "text": "Vinnie flipped it back. The car hugged the track like a cat on a heater.",
   "s": 37.241,
   "e": 40.317
  },
  {
   "text": "Henrietta got the spare wing. She reached the hot-dog stand.",
   "s": 40.517,
   "e": 43.361
  }
 ],
